31	// [About UTC and local time zone]:
32	// In most cases, `number.parseDate` will treat input data string as local time
33	// (except time zone is specified in time string). And `format.formateTime` returns
34	// local time by default. option.useUTC is false by default. This design has
35	// considered these common cases:
36	// (1) Time that is persistent in server is in UTC, but it is needed to be displayed
37	// in local time by default.
38	// (2) By default, the input data string (e.g., '2011-01-02') should be displayed
39	// as its original time, without any time difference.
40	
